{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Tomorrow War appealed to me because its science fiction premise connects with my earlier interest in Star Trek: The Next Generation.",
    "That was the only recommendation with a recognizable connection strong enough for me to choose it now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Spectre's spy thriller premise did not match the science fiction interest guiding my choice right now; action alone was not enough.",
    "Mozart in the Jungle's focus on musicians did not connect with that interest, while Let There Be Light and the unidentified items gave me too little evidence to judge a match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in Star Trek seems to have been interpreted too broadly as interest in other entertainment, regardless of its premise.",
    "If excitement was the connection behind Spectre, that connection was too broad: I was drawn to the science fiction premise of The Tomorrow War."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The science fiction connection mattered more to my choice than a general resemblance as something to watch.",
    "Most of my past interactions are unidentified here, so they do not establish what I liked about those items; my skips of unidentified recommendations reflect uncertainty rather than dislike of their content."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The Tomorrow War captured my clearest visible interest in science fiction, but the other choices lacked a convincing connection or enough information for me to assess one."
}"}
